Cell[TextData[{
 "These probabilities are intuitively too high, particularly when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"m", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "821e7306-467b-4477-8793-41a91b66b7df"],
 ". I think the problem is that if you think of 32 trials as a \
macro-experiment, we ran it once and got a macro-failure (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"m", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "cbb578db-680b-4807-b2b1-5687bc3f4529"],
 "), which doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t tell us much about what would happen if \
we ran it again, hence the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "2"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c0f2ad4-3080-47d8-b0dd-afa4c8053969"],
 " ish.  But once we get to 4 successes, things look very optimistic, 97% \
chance of at least one success in a re-run. I guess I could run some simple \
simulations."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.994000377571185*^9, 3.994000388631625*^9}, {
  3.99400451773669*^9, 3.9940045361559343`*^9}, {3.99400705014863*^9, 
  3.9940071642330923`*^9}, {3.994010649879244*^9, 3.994010650581222*^9}, {
  3.994010684722912*^9, 
  3.9940106991822577`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"27474776-874f-4e8b-a090-\
c9966c9f9811"],

